{
  "id": 490160346,
  "iid": 25150,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "NAS-5GS: Parse URSP Regular expression traffic descriptor",
  "description": "## Summary\n\nAdd parsing for the Regular expression traffic descriptor component (type 0x92) in URSP rules, which was previously showing \"IE not dissected yet\".\n\n## Problem\n\nThe traffic descriptor parser (`de_nas_5gs_ursp_traff_desc`) is missing a `case 0x92` handler. When this type is encountered, the `default` branch displays \"IE not dissected yet\" and abandons parsing of all subsequent components in the same TD block.\n\nNote: The spec comment for this type already exists in the source code (between case 0x91 and case 0xa0), but the actual `case 0x92:` was never added.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added `case 0x92` to the traffic descriptor switch statement\n- Parses: 1-byte length field + variable-length UTF-8 string\n- Added 2 new `hf` field declarations and registrations\n\n## Specification Reference\n\n3GPP TS 24.526 Section 5.2:\n\n> For \"regular expression type\", the traffic descriptor component value field shall be encoded as a sequence of one octet regular expression length field and a regular expression value of variable size. The regular expression value field shall take the form of Extended Regular Expressions (ERE) as defined in chapter 9 in IEEE 1003.1-2004 Part 1.\n\n## Testing\n\nVerified with pcap file containing regular expression `.*\\.example\\.com`:\n\n- **Before:** `IE not dissected yet`\n- **After:** `Regular expression length: 16` / `Regular expression: .*\\.example\\.com`\n\n\nReproduction pcap: [TD_0x92_regex.pcap](https://gitlab.com/-/project/82634231/uploads/3cddecd4fc8e3a87de37597c84527383/TD_0x92_regex.pcap)",
  "state": "merged",
